# --- AI workflow scaffold ---------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is GENERATED. A generated file that is committed goes stale
# silently and is then trusted, which is worse than not having it at all.

# Context packs for AI agents: regenerated by tools/pack.py.
context/

# Code map: regenerated by tools/codemap.py, and large.
docs/codemap.html

# Window captures taken by tools/shot.py so the agent can look at the app.
.claude/shots/

# Run logs.
logs/

# Symbol index, if universal-ctags is in use.
tags

__pycache__/

# Per-machine Claude settings. .claude/settings.json IS tracked -- it is the
# project's permissions and hooks, and every machine wants the same ones.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local shortcut, not part of the project.
*.lnk

# Bulk port: generated plan and run log.
context/port-plan.json
port.log

# --- NOT published -----------------------------------------------------
# This repository is public, and these are the project's own reasoning rather
# than the application: design arguments, the session journal, machine-specific
# deployment detail, and the agent configuration. Felix's decision, 2026-10-14,
# after the v2026.10.14 release made the repository findable.
#
# They stay ON DISK and are excluded from a shipped copy anyway - deploy.py has
# always had docs/ and .claude/ in DEV_DIRS and SKIP_DIRS, so no reader ever
# received them. What changes is only that they are no longer in git.
#
# TWO THINGS TO KNOW. The copies already pushed remain in the HISTORY and are
# recoverable from any clone - nothing is lost by this, and nothing is
# un-published by it either. And from here on doc changes are NOT versioned
# anywhere: the journal, the gotchas and the decisions are the project's memory,
# and they now live on one disk with no backup, which is the exact situation git
# was adopted to end on 2026-09-11. A private repository is the fix and this is
# not it.
docs/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
ROADMAP.md

